# Gate step 1321-2ixp — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. A Windows checkout cannot express the executable bit:
# core.filemode is false there and a NEW file stages as 100644 whatever it is.
# scripts/salvage-dirty-worktree.sh is how work leaves such a host, and by the
# time a relaying host sees the ref the mode is just what the tree says —
# nothing distinguishes "100644 on purpose" from "the substrate could not say
# otherwise". Snapshot time is the LAST moment anyone knows the bit was meant.
#
# MEASURED: scripts/test-windows-host-lane-refusal.sh and its controls arrived
# through a salvage relay at 100644. Every ./build.sh --check passed for a day
# of Linux lands, and the v56.9.20.1 release gate refused
# litmus:windows-host-lane-refusal step 1 (`test -x`) 45 minutes in, on a defect
# a one-second decider could have named.
#
# WHY NOT THE RELAY SIDE. Restoring there fixes the file in front of you and
# leaves the NEXT Windows salvage carrying the same defect — ff82d1001 did
# exactly that for one file, which is why this row stayed open after it. This
# row's own next_action says so in as many words.
#
# THE NEGATIVE CONTROL IS THE ARM THAT MATTERS. Shebang is the signal, so a file
# WITHOUT one must keep 100644 and must not be named as restored. Without that
# arm the tool could flip every file it stages and arm 1 would still pass — a
# salvage that silently makes data files executable inside a recovery copy is
# editing the worktree it exists to preserve. Mutation-proven: dropping the
# shebang test reds it, naming data.yaml.
#
# AND ARM 3 EXISTS BECAUSE ARMS 1 AND 2 RUN A BLOCK EXTRACTED FROM THE TOOL. A
# tool that lost the block would make them VACUOUS rather than red; arm 3 fails
# when the extraction finds nothing, which is the only way the first two can
# stop testing the product without saying so. Mutation-proven: deleting the
# block scores 1/4, not 4/4.
#
# NEEDS NO WINDOWS HOST. `git update-index --chmod=-x` reproduces exactly what a
# core.filemode=false checkout produces, which is how this row's controlled
# pairs were measured throughout.
#
# STEP_SECOND_REGIME (1302-7j8p): RUN, not inferred — the four arms were
# executed on darwin on the host that carries this change.
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-09-22 darwin ok:salvage-exec-bits:4/4"

STEP_DESC="Checking a salvage snapshot restores the exec bit for shebang files (1321-2ixp)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-salvage-preserves-exec-bits.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the salvage no longer restores the executable bit at snapshot time, or restores it for files that never had a shebang (1321-2ixp) — a 1/4 means the restore block is GONE and the first two arms tested nothing; a 3/4 with data.yaml named means the shebang test was dropped and the tool is now editing the copy it exists to preserve"
STEP_OK="Work leaving a Windows host keeps the executable bit it was meant to have"
